  "runtime": "Node 22.22.0, Linux x64",
  "method": "Identical package-lock and installed dependency graph; renderer built with electron-vite (renderer target) on each revision and measured with scripts/check-renderer-bundle.mjs accounting. The watcher dock and attach dialog closures exclude every entry, workbench and detached-chat chunk, and the attach dialog also excludes chunks it shares with the dock.",
  "notes": [
    "foundation: watcher event and result validators join the deferred server-event schema chunk; 841 bytes reach each first-load route.",
    "renderer: eager wiring is the link index, the per-chat dock record, the chip, the dock and attach hosts, the live-phase store, the timeline divider and check model and the composer lock; the dock UI and the attach dialog stay in WatcherDock-* and WatcherAttachDialog-*.",
    "entryCss grows by 70 bytes and stays within its existing ceiling.",
    "Small changes on unrelated deferred chunks are import metadata for helpers (dialog shell, elapsed timing) that Rollup now shares with the watcher chunks.",
    "After merging v0.0.73 (e165a0a), mergedMainBaselineBytes is that revision and mergedBytes the merged branch, built from the same package-lock. Only deferredTasksViewJavaScript needed more room: v0.0.73 measures exactly its 21,126-byte budget and the Work tab nesting adds 6 bytes.",
    "Review fixes: reviewFixBaselineBytes is c17cbf0 (before the server and renderer review fixes) and reviewFixBytes the branch after both, built from the same package-lock. The dock grows by 5,898 bytes (sheet presentation with scrim and composer clearance, user-only motion, focus restoration, Resume refusal reasons, the floating send menu, one-time card entrances); the attach dialog by 958 bytes (link id reuse across ambiguous timeouts). First-load routes grow by 2,660 (workbench) and 2,625 (detached chat) bytes for the dock record's sheet and storage handling, the chip's collapsed live region, the stable linked-chat list and the shared schema-free agent label. The thread actions menu no longer pulls the watcher schema chunk. Budgets were raised by exactly the bytes they were exceeded.",
    "Wave 2 renderer: wave2BaselineBytes is 872e420bb (wave 1 renderer, scheduler and contract pass) and wave2Bytes the branch after the wave 2 renderer work, both built on macOS with Node 22.23.2 from the same package-lock (sizes are identical on every platform). The dock grows by 975 bytes (resolved findings below open ones, the declined-commands note, the automatic-sending menu item and state word, the usage line); the attach dialog by 536 bytes (the automatic-sending switch). First-load routes and core grow by 35 bytes for the shared Switch's optional description link. The baseline already measured 372 bytes over the attach budget and 28 over the core budget from the contract pass, so those caps were raised by that overshoot plus this growth; the others by exactly this growth."
  ],
